.TH ABI\-INSPECT 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.3.2" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
abi\-inspect \- list an ABI's functions, events and errors with selectors/topics, flag selector
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
abi\-inspect [FILE]
FILE (or stdin): ABI JSON (array or {"abi": [...]}, e.g. a compiler artifact) or one signature per line.
Prints every item's canonical signature with selector/topic, selector_collisions, and interfaces:
ERC\-165, ERC\-20, ERC\-721 (+Metadata, Enumerable), ERC\-1155 with complete/missing and the interface_id.
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
collisions, and report which ERC\-165 / ERC\-20 interfaces it implements (ids recomputed), offline.
.nf
.RS 2
  abi\-inspect token.abi.json
  abi\-inspect < signatures.txt
.RE
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
No flags. Input is read from stdin or the arguments shown in SYNOPSIS.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
.nf
.RS 2
  abi\-inspect token.abi.json
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
0
last status ok
.TP
2
last status bad_input
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ abi\-inspect "$R/recipes/fixtures/evm/erc20\-plus\-collision.txt"
# exit 0, last status: ok
$ echo '[' | abi\-inspect
# exit 2, last status: bad_input
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
